- **Finding:** The earlier US-02 Colombia handoff case expected the former Summary placeholder heading `Resumen`. US-03 now renders the approved Summary heading `Revisa tu cotización`.
- **Correction:** The Developer updated the handoff test to verify the Summary heading, selected Ruta plan and same-country plan-change link.
- **Resolution evidence:** The full 22-case Playwright suite passed against the isolated static Compose app. This finding required no production behavior change.
- **History:** The first full run against Angular `ng serve` had 19/22 pass. Two other API 404 assertions received the dev server's SPA fallback. The static-host rerun confirmed both expected 404s and resolved this finding.

## Environment limitations and run history

The initial broad browser run used Angular `ng serve`, which returned its SPA fallback for two unmatched `/api/form-configurations` and `/api/plans` requests that the existing tests expect to return 404. The full suite then passed 22/22 against the isolated static Compose deployment, which confirmed the production-style API responses. The dedicated US-03 terms API boundary test also passed against Strapi for its generated-route, query and method cases.

An initial QA test draft had two incorrect assertions: it expected Colombia terms before the deliberately simulated failed read was retried and assumed document masking removed punctuation. Both assertions were corrected. An initial broad-suite invocation after the isolated dev servers had been stopped returned connection-refused errors. The servers were restarted for the dev-server run, then the complete static Compose run passed. These test and environment issues were not application defects.

Native screen-reader and operating-system high-contrast checks were not run. The browser verification covers keyboard operation, accessible names, live status text, and 320 px reflow. No automated axe scan was run.

## Approved copy revision re-verification, 2026-11-22

The QA flow now checks that the retired fictitious-data introduction and identity-number hint are absent from Details; Summary exposes the `Resultado de prueba` group and `Pagar` action without the former demonstration heading, no-real-charge sentence, or `Simular pago` action; and the approved receipt contains no country name or standalone no-charge sentence. These are copy acceptance checks, not a new QA defect. The Colombia and Chile full quote flows each exercised rejection, retry with preserved owner and selected plan, approval, and reload of the same receipt. Both passed on the refreshed local Compose app at `127.0.0.1:8080`. The isolated terms API, direct-route prerequisite, and interrupted-check reload tests also passed in the same five-test run.

During the first follow-up attempt, the new Details copy checks completed, but the CO flow timed out because the QA helper expected the former `Ejemplo Motor` option while the refreshed CO seed offers `Mazda` and `Chevrolet`. The test helper now selects the first configured brand option. This was test fixture drift, not an application defect. The focused rerun passed 2/2 country flows, then the complete dedicated suite passed 5/5. `prettier --check e2e/us03-qa.spec.ts` passed before the reruns.

## Approved terminal quote revision re-verification, 2026-11-22

Added independent browser coverage in `e2e/us03-terminal-qa.spec.ts` for AC-US03-R01 through R03. The final run used Chrome against the fresh isolated production Compose stack at `127.0.0.1:18084`. In Colombia and Chile, Chrome approved a quote and compared the stored masked review, plan and final price after reload with the active country's quote-content requests stubbed unavailable; the app issued no such request. Direct Details and Plans URLs and browser Back/Forward all resolved to the same terminal Summary without input, selection, Pay, edit or plan-change controls. Switching to the other country still opened its own empty Details step. Chile's terminal receipt reflowed at 320 CSS px without horizontal overflow.

Both countries also exercised an injected receipt-key deletion failure: the error was announced, focus stayed on the restart control, and reload restored the original terminal receipt. Keyboard retry cleared the active country's prior entered data, selected plan and receipt, opened same-country Details with focus on its heading, and prevented the old Summary history entry from restoring the receipt. A subsequent approval created a different reference. A legacy version 1 reference-only Colombia receipt remained terminal and reset successfully. The existing rejection, edit, plan retention and retry-to-approval cases passed for both countries in the same full-suite run.

The first focused terminal run passed the legacy case but four country cases failed because the test compared multiline `innerText()` with Playwright's normalized `toHaveText()` representation. After correcting that comparison, an expanded run found two more test-only reset expectation failures: Angular's configured select placeholder has DOM value `0: null`, so the tests were updated to assert the selected placeholder label instead. No application defect was indicated by either test-authoring mismatch. The corrected focused run passed 5/5; the final full browser suite passed 27/27. The final tests include keyboard reset and focus checks. This run did not modify CMS content.

## QA recommendation

The US-03 base scope, copy revision and terminal quote revision passed dedicated browser, CMS integration, unit and full cross-story browser coverage. US03-QA-01 is resolved with evidence. No blocking implementation defect was reproduced. Native screen-reader and operating-system high-contrast checks remain unverified.
import { expect, test, type Page } from "@playwright/test";

type Scenario = {
  country: "co" | "cl";
  otherCountry: "co" | "cl";
  viewport: { width: number; height: number };
  vehicleLabel: "Placa" | "Patente";
  identityLabel: "Número de documento" | "RUT";
  currency: "COP" | "CLP";
  price: string;
  identitySuffix: string;
};

const scenarios: Scenario[] = [
  {
    country: "co",
    otherCountry: "cl",
    viewport: { width: 1280, height: 900 },
    vehicleLabel: "Placa",
    identityLabel: "Número de documento",
    currency: "COP",
    price: "129.900,50",
    identitySuffix: "8301",
  },
  {
    country: "cl",
    otherCountry: "co",
    viewport: { width: 320, height: 844 },
    vehicleLabel: "Patente",
    identityLabel: "RUT",
    currency: "CLP",
    price: "24.900",
    identitySuffix: "8302",
  },
];

function person(country: Scenario["country"], label: string) {
  return `QA Terminal ${country.toUpperCase()} ${label}`;
}

async function fillDetails(
  page: Page,
  scenario: Scenario,
  label: string,
  identitySuffix: string,
) {
  await expect(
    page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Datos para cotizar" }),
  ).toBeVisible();
  await page
    .getByLabel("Nombre del titular")
    .fill(person(scenario.country, label));
  if (scenario.country === "co") {
    await page
      .getByLabel("Tipo de documento")
      .selectOption({ label: "Cédula de ciudadanía" });
    await page.getByLabel("Placa").fill("QA-CO-03");
  } else {
    await page.getByLabel("Patente").fill("QA-CL-03");
  }
  await page
    .getByLabel(scenario.identityLabel)
    .fill(`FICTITIOUS-ID-${identitySuffix}`);
  await page.getByLabel("Fecha de nacimiento").fill("1990-02-10");
  await page.getByLabel("Año del vehículo").fill("2021");
  await page.getByLabel("Marca").selectOption({ index: 1 });
  await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Continuar" }).click();
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(new RegExp(`/${scenario.country}/quote/plans$`));
}

async function approveQuote(
  page: Page,
  scenario: Scenario,
  label: string,
  identitySuffix: string,
) {
  await fillDetails(page, scenario, label, identitySuffix);
  const plan = page.getByRole("radio", { name: "Esencial", exact: true });
  await expect(plan).toBeVisible();
  await plan.check();
  await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Continuar" }).click();
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(
    new RegExp(`/${scenario.country}/quote/summary$`),
  );
  await page
    .getByRole("checkbox", { name: "Acepto los términos y condiciones" })
    .check();
  await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Pagar" }).click();
  await expect(
    page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Pago aprobado" }),
  ).toBeVisible();
  return readReceipt(page);
}

async function readReceipt(page: Page) {
  const reference = (
    await page.getByText(/^DEMO-[A-F0-9]{24}$/).textContent()
  )?.trim();
  if (!reference) throw new Error("Approved quote reference was not rendered");
  const review = page.locator('[aria-labelledby="receipt-review-heading"]');
  const plan = page.locator('[aria-labelledby="receipt-plan-heading"]');
  return {
    reference,
    review: await review.innerText(),
    plan: await plan.innerText(),
  };
}

async function expectTerminal(
  page: Page,
  scenario: Scenario,
  saved: Awaited<ReturnType<typeof readReceipt>>,
) {
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(
    new RegExp(`/${scenario.country}/quote/summary$`),
  );
  await expect(
    page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Pago aprobado" }),
  ).toBeFocused();
  await expect(page.getByText(saved.reference, { exact: true })).toBeVisible();
  const review = await page
    .locator('[aria-labelledby="receipt-review-heading"]')
    .innerText();
  const plan = await page
    .locator('[aria-labelledby="receipt-plan-heading"]')
    .innerText();
  expect(review.replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim()).toBe(
    saved.review.replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim(),
  );
  expect(plan.replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim()).toBe(
    saved.plan.replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim(),
  );
  await expect(page.locator("input, select, textarea")).toHaveCount(0);
  await expect(page.getByRole("radio")).toHaveCount(0);
  await expect(page.getByRole("button", { name: "Pagar" })).toHaveCount(0);
  await expect(page.getByRole("link", { name: "Editar datos" })).toHaveCount(0);
  await expect(page.getByRole("link", { name: "Cambiar plan" })).toHaveCount(0);
}

for (const scenario of scenarios) {
  test(`T-US03-R01/R02: ${scenario.country.toUpperCase()} terminal route guard preserves captured approval`, async ({
    page,
  }) => {
    await page.setViewportSize(scenario.viewport);
    await page.goto(`/${scenario.country}/quote/details`);
    const saved = await approveQuote(
      page,
      scenario,
      "Original",
      scenario.identitySuffix,
    );

    const review = page.locator('[aria-labelledby="receipt-review-heading"]');
    const identity = (
      await review
        .locator("dd")
        .filter({ hasText: scenario.identitySuffix })
        .innerText()
    ).trim();
    expect(identity).toMatch(new RegExp(`^[•…-]*${scenario.identitySuffix}$`));
    expect(identity).not.toContain("FICTITIOUS");
    await expect(
      review.getByText(person(scenario.country, "Original"), { exact: true }),
    ).toBeVisible();
    await expect(
      page.locator('[aria-labelledby="receipt-plan-heading"]'),
    ).toContainText(new RegExp(`${scenario.currency}.*${scenario.price}`));

    const blockedRequests: string[] = [];
    await page.route(
      `**/api/quote-content/v1/${scenario.country}/**`,
      async (route) => {
        blockedRequests.push(route.request().url());
        await route.fulfill({ status: 503, body: "unavailable" });
      },
    );
    await page.reload();
    await expectTerminal(page, scenario, saved);
    expect(
      await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.scrollWidth),
    ).toBeLessThanOrEqual(scenario.viewport.width);

    for (const step of ["details", "plans"] as const) {
      await page.goto(`/${scenario.country}/quote/${step}`);
      await expectTerminal(page, scenario, saved);
    }
    await page.goBack();
    await expectTerminal(page, scenario, saved);
    await page.goForward();
    await expectTerminal(page, scenario, saved);
    expect(blockedRequests).toEqual([]);

    await page.goto(`/${scenario.otherCountry}/quote/details`);
    await expect(
      page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Datos para cotizar" }),
    ).toBeVisible();
    await expect(page.getByLabel("Nombre del titular")).toHaveValue("");
    await expect(page.getByText(saved.reference, { exact: true })).toHaveCount(
      0,
    );
    await page.goto(`/${scenario.country}/quote/details`);
    await expectTerminal(page, scenario, saved);
    expect(blockedRequests).toEqual([]);
  });

  test(`T-US03-R03: ${scenario.country.toUpperCase()} restart clears terminal quote and permits a new approval`, async ({
    page,
  }) => {
    await page.setViewportSize({ width: 1280, height: 900 });
    await page.goto(`/${scenario.country}/quote/details`);
    const saved = await approveQuote(
      page,
      scenario,
      "Original",
      scenario.identitySuffix,
    );
    const restart = page.getByRole("button", {
      name: "Iniciar una nueva cotización",
    });

    await page.evaluate((country) => {
      const removeItem = Storage.prototype.removeItem;
      Storage.prototype.removeItem = function (key: string) {
        if (key === `quote-receipt-v1:${country}`) {
          throw new DOMException(
            "Simulated receipt cleanup failure",
            "SecurityError",
          );
        }
        removeItem.call(this, key);
      };
    }, scenario.country);
    await restart.focus();
    await page.keyboard.press("Enter");
    await expect(page.getByRole("alert")).toContainText(
      "No pudimos iniciar una nueva cotización",
    );
    await expect(restart).toBeFocused();
    await expect(
      page.getByText(saved.reference, { exact: true }),
    ).toBeVisible();

    await page.reload();
    await expectTerminal(page, scenario, saved);
    const retryRestart = page.getByRole("button", {
      name: "Iniciar una nueva cotización",
    });
    await retryRestart.focus();
    await page.keyboard.press("Enter");
    await expect(page).toHaveURL(
      new RegExp(`/${scenario.country}/quote/details$`),
    );
    await expect(
      page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Datos para cotizar" }),
    ).toBeFocused();
    await expect(page.getByLabel("Nombre del titular")).toHaveValue("");
    await expect(page.getByLabel(scenario.identityLabel)).toHaveValue("");
    await expect(page.getByLabel(scenario.vehicleLabel)).toHaveValue("");
    await expect(page.getByLabel("Fecha de nacimiento")).toHaveValue("");
    await expect(page.getByLabel("Año del vehículo")).toHaveValue("");
    await expect(page.getByLabel("Marca").locator("option:checked")).toHaveText(
      "Selecciona una opción",
    );
    await expect(
      page.getByLabel("El auto tiene accesorios adicionales"),
    ).not.toBeChecked();
    if (scenario.country === "co") {
      await expect(
        page.getByLabel("Tipo de documento").locator("option:checked"),
      ).toHaveText("Selecciona una opción");
    }

    const storageAfterReset = await page.evaluate((country) => {
      const draft = sessionStorage.getItem(`quote-draft-v1:${country}`);
      return {
        receipt: sessionStorage.getItem(`quote-receipt-v1:${country}`),
        plan: sessionStorage.getItem(`quote-plan-v1:${country}`),
        draft: draft ? JSON.parse(draft) : null,
      };
    }, scenario.country);
    expect(storageAfterReset.receipt).toBeNull();
    expect(storageAfterReset.plan).toBeNull();
    expect(JSON.stringify(storageAfterReset.draft)).not.toContain(
      person(scenario.country, "Original"),
    );
    expect(JSON.stringify(storageAfterReset.draft)).not.toContain(
      `FICTITIOUS-ID-${scenario.identitySuffix}`,
    );

    await page.goto(`/${scenario.country}/quote/summary`);
    await expect(page).toHaveURL(
      new RegExp(`/${scenario.country}/quote/details$`),
    );
    await expect(page.getByLabel("Nombre del titular")).toHaveValue("");
    await expect(page.getByText(saved.reference, { exact: true })).toHaveCount(
      0,
    );
    await page.reload();
    await expect(page.getByLabel("Nombre del titular")).toHaveValue("");
    await expect(page.getByText(saved.reference, { exact: true })).toHaveCount(
      0,
    );

    await page.goBack();
    await expect(page).toHaveURL(
      new RegExp(`/${scenario.country}/quote/details$`),
    );
    await expect(page.getByText(saved.reference, { exact: true })).toHaveCount(
      0,
    );
    await page.goForward();
    await expect(page).toHaveURL(
      new RegExp(`/${scenario.country}/quote/details$`),
    );
    await expect(page.getByLabel("Nombre del titular")).toHaveValue("");

    await fillDetails(page, scenario, "New", "8401");
    const plan = page.getByRole("radio", { name: "Esencial", exact: true });
    await expect(plan).not.toBeChecked();
    await plan.check();
    await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Continuar" }).click();
    await expect(page).toHaveURL(
      new RegExp(`/${scenario.country}/quote/summary$`),
    );
    const consent = page.getByRole("checkbox", {
      name: "Acepto los términos y condiciones",
    });
    await expect(consent).not.toBeChecked();
    await consent.check();
    await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Pagar" }).click();
    await expect(
      page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Pago aprobado" }),
    ).toBeVisible();
    const replacement = await readReceipt(page);
    expect(replacement.reference).not.toBe(saved.reference);
    await expect(
      page
        .locator('[aria-labelledby="receipt-review-heading"]')
        .getByText(person(scenario.country, "New"), { exact: true }),
    ).toBeVisible();
  });
}

test("T-US03-R01/R03: legacy reference-only receipt stays terminal and can restart", async ({
  page,
}) => {
  await page.goto("/");
  const reference = "DEMO-" + "A".repeat(24);
  await page.evaluate((number) => {
    sessionStorage.setItem(
      "quote-receipt-v1:co",
